                <pb facs="0107" n="57" sameAs="frus:frus1894/pg57"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Thompson to Mr. Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Rio
                                de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-04-12"><hi rendition="#italic">April 12,
                        1894</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Thompson reports that the governor of Rio Grande do Sul has telegraphed to
                    the Brazilian foreign office the news of a serious defeat and great loss
                    sustained at Port Alegre by the rebels, who took to their vessels and, being
                    advised of the approach of the squadron sent by the Brazilian Government, fled
                    in haste.</p>
            </div>
